                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Reasoning About Knowledge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262562003/reasoning-about-knowledge/"} ISBN:9780262562003
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %blockquote
              %p p. 35: “in a precise sense the S5 properties completely characterize our definition of knowledge”
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Y.+Halpern"}> Joseph Y. Halpern
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Should knowledge entail belief?
                  %strong 25
                  5 (1996) 483-494
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/30226583"} jstor:30226583
                  %a{:href => "https://philpapers.org/rec/HALSKE"} philpapers:HALSKE
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#Fitting07
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Melvin+Fitting"}> Melvin Fitting
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Logics of Knowlege
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Modal proof theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Handbook of Modal Logic
                  %strong 3
                  (2007) 85-183
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S1570-2464(07)80005-X"} doi:10.1016/S1570-2464(07)80005-X
                  %a{:href => "https://cgi.csc.liv.ac.uk/~frank/MLHandbook/"} book webpage
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %blockquote
              %p
                pp. 121: “What standard logics of knowledge capture is not actual knowledge, but potential knowledge — what one is entitled to know. The switch to potential knowledge means we drop all considerations of complexity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
                It is easy to see that, under such an assumption, a knowledge modality should be a normal modal operator. But, what else should be required?
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
